node=browser=fnv1a32:a45ba9ac` unchanged throughout.** The merged tree hash `66c4ce86` is **byte-identical to the gated tree**, so what shipped is the commit that was gated (never a fresh resolution). Review: `reviews/half-stamped-reel-refusal.md`. 🕳️ **F-2476-1 — THE RUNNER WITHHELD ITS ONLY SCREENSHOTS, AND A "WITHHELD" LINE IS NOT AN ERROR LINE (non-blocking, DISCHARGED in this drain).** `lane-runner-v3` printed `withheld baseline-dirty path: reviews/shots-half-stamped-reel-refusal/*.png` and `withheld 2 baseline ownership collision(s)` at the very TAIL of the run log, **after** its own `READY-FOR-GATES` block whose `Evidence:` line cites those same screenshots. The withhold is CORRECT — a runner must not commit evidence whose baseline another task owns — but the consequence is a slice that reports evidence and has **none in any commit**: both PNGs lived only in the untracked lane worktree, one `git clean -fd` from gone (Mistake #11 / RETENTION LAW). Landed here path-scoped, 985,902 B + 1,540,021 B. **Nothing was lost because the drain went looking.** ➡️ **READ THE RUN-LOG TAIL PAST THE REPORT BLOCK: a withheld path is an owed `git add`, not a diagnostic.** ⓘ **F-2476-2 — `test:node-guards` deliberately NOT run, stated so the next reader need not re-derive it:** §3 keys that battery on `src/sim/` · `src/systems/` · `src/entities/`, and this diff is `src/game/Game.ts` + `src/ui/LanternShow.ts` — watch-path routing and a UI accessor, moving no behaviour the sim replays. The rule is keyed on PATHS precisely so this is not a judgement call, so it was followed as written rather than widened on a hunch; the unchanged `fnv1a32:a45ba9ac` determinism triple corroborates.
