tasks/BACKLOG.md:107:🔴 **F-2471-1 — THE BROWSER'S ERA REFUSAL IS UNREACHABLE FOR THE EXACT TAPE SHAPE IT NAMES, AND ITS GUARD IS RED ON MAIN TODAY (s2471, 2026-09-03; PRE-EXISTING, NOT the tape-resume slice — CONTROL-PROVEN).** `e2e/agent-reels.spec.ts:301` ("plain town board WATCH gives a half-stamped reel its honest unstamped-era refusal") FAILS on BOTH projects: it expects `data-era-refused="true"` and receives `"false"`, with the show reading `data-playback="playing"` — **the reel is PLAYED, not refused.** 🔬 **CONTROL, and it is what keeps this out of the drain's account: the identical failure with an identical fingerprint reproduces on `main`'s own worktree with none of the merged files present** (rc=1, 2 failed, same line 307, same expected/received). §3's "fingerprint-matched to known-reds with proof". 🔑 **DIAGNOSED BY READING, and the mechanism is exact and one line wide.** `src/game/Game.ts:7091` computes the refusal correctly — `!meta?.engineHash || meta.era !== engineEra.era || !engineEraIncludes(...)` — and is the ONLY site that computes it. The router seventeen lines above, `Game.ts:7033`, reads `if (hasAgentOrders && tape.meta?.engineHash && tape.meta.era)`. **A tape carrying an `engineHash` and NO `era` — precisely the "half-stamped" shape 7091 exists to catch — fails that guard and falls through to the LEGACY human-tape replay path, which never computes `eraRefusal` and simply plays the reel. The router and the refusal are complements that overlap wrongly: the gate diverts the case away from the only code that can judge it.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: this is NOT a ranking or data defect.** The door's server-side era filter (`functions/api/standings.ts`) is untouched and `test:stats` proves it green at 215/215 across both storage paths, so no unstamped reel can rank. The realised cost is **honesty on a player-visible surface** — the Lantern Show plays a reel that does not announce its era instead of showing the refusal the owner's 2026-08-31 era ruling promises — plus a **red sitting in a mandated e2e battery**, which is exactly how a red decays into one nobody investigates (F-1460-1). 🚫 **Deliberately NOT fixed in the drain: `src/game/Game.ts` and `src/ui/LanternShow.ts` are outside the tape-resume master's TOUCH-ONLY list, and a routing change on the true-reel driver needs its own gate.** ➡️ **PRICED AND FIRE-AUTHORABLE: the cure is one condition at `Game.ts:7033` (route on `hasAgentOrders` alone and let 7091 judge the stamp), and the e2e that must go green is ALREADY WRITTEN and ALREADY FAILING — so the corrective needs no new test, only the fix and its gate.** 💡 **REUSABLE: when a guard's condition and its ROUTER are written as complements, check the overlap rather than each half — a refusal that its own dispatcher can never reach is a refusal the factory does not have, and it reads as correct in every review of the file that contains it.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:108:🔴 **F-2467-1 — TWO ANSWERED OWNER QUESTIONS SAT ON THE DESK AS "AWAITING A WORD" FOR FOUR DAYS, AND TWO INDEPENDENT SELECTORS EACH CERTIFIED THEM OPEN — CORRECTLY (s2467, 2026-09-03, MEASURED, LIVE NOT LATENT, CURED AT THE LEDGER).** Found while reconciling a desk COUNT; it turned out to be a desk STATE error. **`F-SHOW-0830a`** (should the flagship boss punish static play?) and **`F-SHOW-0830b`** (the flagship reel reads fake) were **ANSWERED by the owner on 2026-08-30** — verbatim *"yes, all of this. lets improve this"* — **and the answer has fully SHIPPED**. 🔑 **TWO ORTHOGONAL MECHANISMS, BOTH BEING RIGHT: (a) POSITION OF THE CLAIM.** The closure was written into the F-SHOW-0830 row’s **BODY** (`✅ BOTH FORKS ANSWERED …`), and `desk-state-audit`’s subject-first rule reads only the first `90` chars — **deliberately**, because a body claim is not a state claim; the standing measurement that body closures run **~62.5% FALSE** is precisely why that rule exists. **(b) THE ID REGEX CANNOT EXPRESS THE ITEMS.** `FINDING_ONE = /\bF-[A-Z0-9]+(?:-[A-Z0-9]+)*-\d+\b/` requires a trailing `-<digits>`, so **`F-SHOW-0830a` and `F-SHOW-0830b` match NOTHING** and both collapse onto a single `F-SHOW-0830` row keyed to neither. Two honest tools partitioned on orthogonal keys, leaving a hole neither can report — **F-2358-1’s lesson exactly**. 👥 **THIS IS THE THIRD MEMBER OF F-2464-2’s FAMILY AND IS CITED AS SUCH RATHER THAN CLAIMED AS NEW:** that finding named (1) a closure tick behind another emoji (`lead.startsWith('✅')`, `0.19%` of rows) and (2) a compound desk heading hiding its second id. **This is (3): a desk id whose SHAPE the parser cannot express.** ⚖️ **The difference that matters is severity: F-2464-2 is LATENT and was filed priced. THIS ONE FIRED** — it kept two answered questions on the owner’s desk for four days. 🔎 **VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY OF THE BODY TEXT, because that text is the thing under suspicion:** `specs/embodied-hand.md` is **Status: RATIFIED 2026-08-30**, quotes the owner verbatim, and **every one of its four slices has MERGED** — EH-1 `embodied-build-v2` @`a73790d9a2` (spec law 1 "one door, one hand": a walking hand cannot anchor-build, which is what **absorbs** the 0830a fork), EH-2 `true-reel-harness` @`8c5684def8`, EH-3 `true-reel-show` @`af85497537` (**this IS 0830b option (ii)**, the true renderer the owner asked for by name — *"can we not convert the AI tape to a human watchable tape?"*), EH-4 `gauntlet-heat7-embodied-crown` @`b43df480f3`. **Answered AND delivered**, not merely acknowledged. 🛠️ **CURED AT THE LEDGER, NOT AT THE PARSER** — the F-SHOW-0830 row now **leads `✅` with the bare id inside the 90-char zone**, so `desk-state-audit` reads it **CLOSED**, and both forks are **RETIRED from the desk s2467** with their original text preserved verbatim in place (Retention Law: mark, never erase). ⛔ **`scan()`/`FINDING_ONE` DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED, for F-2464-2’s own priced reason**: `scan()` is imported by `desk-state-audit`, `desk-carryforward-guard` and `ruling-propagation-guard`, and its guard is rooted in `test:node-guards` (**529.8 s floor, F-2166-2**) — which could not be run cleanly, because lane-a held a live gate battery for this fire’s whole duration and **F-2462-1** establishes that a self-contaminated battery manufactures findings. A ledger cure needs no code change and no battery. ⚠️ **MY FIRST EDIT WAS WRONG AND IS RECORDED BECAUSE IT IS THE LESSON:** leading the row with the SUFFIXED ids drove it from `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` to **`UNRECORDED`** — **strictly worse**, since the row lost its subject attribution entirely. **Reverted byte-identically** (`git checkout --`; baseline re-audited back to `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=2 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=48 · UNRECORDED=0`), then I **READ** `rowState`/`scan` (`findings-state-guard.mjs:81–111`) and rebuilt it correct by construction, with the splice REFUSING unless the bare id lands in-zone. **A remedy aimed by intuition at a selector you have not read is how a correct row gets corrupted.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: NOTHING WAS LOST and no owner question ever went unseen.** Desk ITEMS are carried by **SPLICE**, so both texts survived verbatim in every handoff and Robin could always read them; `CLOSED=0` was TRUE under the subject-first rule. The realised cost is that two **answered** items occupied desk space for four days and the headline over-counted. **It is NARROW: exactly `2` of `51` desk ids are inexpressible to the parser** — the other 49 were measured, not assumed. 🚫 **NO GUARD PROPOSED, and the restraint is measured rather than lazy:** *"is this body claim a real closure?"* is a **JUDGEMENT**, so a red would fire on every honest triage row that discusses an outcome and be excused into uselessness inside a week (**F-1460-1**, the `cross-engine` fate). It is the same restraint F-1669-1 took for done-move filenames. **The cure is the ledger row, at the site.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is the sharp half:** the desk’s ITEMS are protected by splice; its **COUNT and its STATE are not**. A number carried by retyping is the one field that can drift, and a state written in a body is a state no instrument reads. **When a ledger row records an outcome, put it in the SUBJECT ZONE in the same commit** — a closure nobody’s parser can see is a closure the factory does not have. ➡️ **UNCLAIMED, AND EXACT:** sweep the board for 🔺/🎭-led rows whose BODY claims a closure (`ANSWERED`/`RULED`/`owner 2026-`) that their SUBJECT ZONE does not state. One grep plus judgement, no new tool. **Verify each against a RATIFIED artifact and shipped hashes, never against the body claim** — that is the ~62.5%-false population by construction.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:115:🟡 **F-2464-2 — A CLOSURE TICK BEHIND ANY OTHER EMOJI IS INVISIBLE TO EVERY CONSUMER OF `scan()`, AND A COMPOUND DESK HEADING HIDES ITS SECOND ID OUTRIGHT (s2464, 2026-09-03, MEASURED, LATENT, FILED PRICED AND DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED).** Two independent selector gaps, found by asking whether the desk I inherited was still true. 🔬 **(1) POSITION, NOT PRESENCE.** `findings-state-guard.mjs:90` decides closure with `lead.startsWith('✅')` — so `⚖️✅ **F-WIN-2 RULED (attended 2026-09-03)**` is read as NEITHER closed NOR open, and `subjectState`'s `fallbackState` re-scan cannot rescue it because it applies the same test. The `struck` arm does not catch it either: that needs `/✅\s*(?:CLOSED|RETIRED)/`, and every one of these rows puts `**F-…` between the tick and the word. **PROVEN BY CONTROL, ground truth = an item the owner ruled TODAY: a desk carrying `F-WIN-2` alone reads `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` with evidence at the very row that rules it.** 📊 **CENSUS, so severity is measured and NOT inflated: of `2,089` BACKLOG rows whose 90-char subject carries an F-id, `390` lead with a bare `✅` and only `4` use the emoji-prefixed form — `0.19%`. This is a RARE house style, not a systematic hole.** ➡️ **THE CURE IS ONE LINE and its blast radius was measured before being recommended, not guessed: widening to `/^[^A-Za-z0-9\s]{1,6}✅/` flips EXACTLY `4` rows, and all four genuinely assert closure — the `F-WIN-2 RULED` row, the `human-tape-true-reel-stamp MERGED … F-SLHP-2 CLOSED` row, the `F-2456-1 — THE DESK LEADS WITH A 🚨 THAT IS DISCHARGED` row, and the `F-E3CF-4 CLOSED` row. Zero false positives. ⓘ **CITED BY CONTENT, NOT COORDINATE, AND THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS ROW PROVES WHY: it named them `L6 · L19 · L71 · L1072`, measured minutes earlier — and then I prepended this very finding to the top of the file, shifting all four by exactly `+2` to `L8 · L21 · L73 · L1074`. The coordinates were WRONG AT THE MOMENT OF WRITING, before any later edit could rot them (F-2449-1: a pointer can be BORN drifted). Re-derive them with `/^[^A-Za-z0-9\s]{1,6}✅/` over the subject zone; the ids are stable and the line numbers are not.**** ⛔ **NOT SHIPPED THIS FIRE, and the restraint is priced rather than timid: `scan()` is imported by `desk-state-audit`, `desk-carryforward-guard` and `ruling-propagation-guard`, and its own guard `findings-state-guard.test.mjs` is rooted in `test:node-guards` (**529.8 s floor, F-2166-2**) — which could not be run cleanly, because lane-a held a live gate battery for this fire's whole duration and F-2462-1 establishes that a self-contaminated battery manufactures findings. **A green I could not trust is worth less than a finding I can.** The next fire on a quiet board lands it in one edit with this blast radius already measured. 🎯 **(2) THE COMPOUND HEADING, which is the half with a live cost today: the inherited desk carries one item headed `F-WIN-1 / F-WIN-2`, and `desk-state-audit` reports ONLY `F-WIN-1` — `F-WIN-2` is absent from its item list entirely, at any verdict.** So even after cure (1), a ruled id inside a shared heading stays invisible. ⚖️ **CONSEQUENCE, and it is F-1600-1 exactly — *a check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again*: `F-WIN-2` WAS RULED by the attended session at `412836942` (option (b)) and the desk audit is structurally unable to say so.** ➡️ **WRITING RULE, which costs nothing and needs no code: give every desk id its OWN `🔺 **F-xxxx-x**` heading, even when two findings share one paragraph of reasoning. A heading is the audit's subject key, not decoration.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is this factory's most-repeated shape on a new axis: both gaps are selectors narrower than the question they are asked. The first keys on WHERE a marker sits rather than WHETHER it is there; the second keys on the FIRST id rather than every id. Neither can fail loudly, because in both cases the miss renders as the desk's ordinary resting state — `OPEN-DESK-ONLY` — which is exactly what a genuinely open item looks like.**
tasks/BACKLOG.md:136:🎞️✅ **human-tape-true-reel-stamp MERGED (s2461, 2026-09-03, `16ed9b222`) — F-SLHP-2 CLOSED: a human standing-order tape can be watched again.** Human run tapes now carry the engine identity that made them (`RunTapeMeta.engineHash` + `era`); a resumed recording RETAINS its original stamp rather than being silently re-stamped by a newer build; stamped order tapes route to true replay and watch to their own event hash; unstamped legacy tapes keep working through the ordinary tape show, so nothing already on a shelf is invalidated. **GATES (merged tree, detached `gate-s2461`, `--workers=1`): tsc rc=0 · build rc=0 17.48 s · 18/18 across tape-01, c7-standing-order-replay, tape-02-lantern-show, same-laws-harvest-parity, desktop AND 390px, zero console/page errors · node-guards 562 pass · power-budget + stats + accounts + mp + task-guards + citations + gate-callers all rc=0.** 🔧 **THREE BOTH-MOVED paths, all resolved by KEEPING BOTH SIDES; the union of main's `viewVersion` validator with the lane's `engineHash`/`era` pair rule weakens neither side.** 🩹 **F-2461-1: the lane's own `c7` assertion used exact `toEqual` and predated `viewVersion`, so it redded on BOTH projects on the merged tree — reconciled to assert all three stamps, and deliberately LEFT as `toEqual` rather than relaxed to `toMatchObject`, because "exactly the declared stamp and no stray field" is what makes the stamped-vs-unstamped routing decidable. Relaxing it would have removed the test's teeth to make a red go away.** 📌 **F-2461-2: era-5 pin `cb321d83` appended (pins 11 → 12) with the cause COUNTED not assumed — main was measured SELF-CONSISTENT at `10c1fa66` FIRST, which is what proves this slice is the only cause; the merged hash was computed independently and matched the guard's message; top-level `engineHash` updated in the same edit (s2460's lesson: appending only the pin leaves the guard red at an earlier assertion).** 📐 **F-2461-3: the `placeBuilding` law pointer re-based 2524–2525 → 2525–2526. The runner PREDICTED this rot and predicted **+12**; measured **+1**. Subject right, magnitude wrong — even a runner reading its own diff cannot compute the shift, because it depends on what lands ABOVE the site. Both range members re-grepped INDEPENDENTLY (the law warns a range is two pointers and only the first is guarded) and eye-checked by reading the lines back.** ⚠️ **F-2461-4 NOT BLOCKING, pre-existing: `fixture-teardown` reds at the art-gitdir 11-dir leak (F-2459-3). In the full battery it reported only that its CHILD `engine-era-guard` had failed, so curing the pin did NOT clear it; run ALONE (547 s) it reds independently at the leak. Not this slice, still open, still taxing every mandated battery.** Review: `reviews/human-tape-true-reel-stamp.md`.
