tasks/BACKLOG.md:183:🏞️ **LANTERN-TRUE-TERRAIN — SHIPPED `c1084e547` (s2453) (2026-09-02).** The owner's playtest-16 complaint answered verbatim ("the map is not displayed but only a schematic view of a grey area is shown. That is a bit disappointing", F-PT16-2). The Lantern Show now draws the contract's REAL ground: `src/ui/TrueReelTerrain.ts` (new, 298 lines) projects elevation, water + fords, cliffs, build pads, rails, stakes, seam anchors, spawn edges and the Night Shift light cycle from the manifest `tileParams` + tape seed — **never from the replay snapshot, which carries no ground**, which is what makes it real rather than decorative. `terrain layout` leaves `TRUE_REEL_PLACEHOLDERS`; **`decorative props` stays, because the scatter is not deterministic** — the master's honesty guard working as written. GATES (merged tree, `--workers=1`, detached `gate-s2453`): tsc clean · build green · **36/36** across agent-reels, reel-deep-links, run3d-lantern-post, tape-02-lantern-show, true-reel-harness, desktop + 390px · zero console/page errors · plain-boot no-debug WATCH path green (Mistake #10) · 12 screenshots + 2 perf JSON in `reviews/shots-lantern-true-terrain/`, eye-checked (Hill Mine terraces + ford read; Night Shift reads dark). 🩹 **REVIEW FIX F-2453-1 — the slice shipped an ABSOLUTE frame-budget pin into the e2e gate and it was REMOVED WITH A NAMED CAUSE (not F-1441-3's forbidden clear-the-red re-pin).** The lane added `(mobile ? 10.2 : 16.9) * 1.15` beside main's load-invariant `liveP95 * 1.15`, faithfully implementing scope 4 — **the master asked for something the law elsewhere forbids**. It was already failing: first gate red 390px `24.90 > 11.73`, re-run red BOTH projects. Measured with the pin neutralised: desktop live 16.60 / reel **10.40** (0.63x), 390px live 25.00 / reel **14.90** (0.60x), and a third run desktop live 41.70 / reel 24.40 (0.59x) — **the reel is 33-41% FASTER than the live map every time, so there is NO regression**; but absolute p95 swung