tasks/BACKLOG.md:533:✅ **F-2316-1 — CURED s2319 at `9852bcbe6` (see F-2319-1, which REFUTES the cure recommended below) — THE LANE RUNNER'S AUTO-COMMIT SWEEPS ANY NEW UNTRACKED `logs/*` FILE, BECAUSE ITS EXCLUDE LIST IS HAND-ENUMERATED; AND POST-CURE THAT SWEEP NO LONGER DIRTIES A TREE — IT SILENTLY DISABLES THE INSTRUMENT (filed by fire s2316 in `reviews/f2315-1.md`; BACKLOG row landed s2317, discharging s2316's recorded deferral).** ⚙️ **THE MECHANISM, RE-VERIFIED AT SOURCE BY s2317 RATHER THAN INHERITED (Mistake #4): `scripts/lane-runner-v3.sh:488` commits lane output with `git add -A -- . ':(exclude).wrangler' ':(exclude)logs/factory-usage.json' ':(exclude)logs/usage-history.jsonl'`** — an `add -A` over the whole worktree minus a **hardcoded list of exactly three paths**, two of which are already `logs/` churn. `logs/guard-stats.jsonl` was born at `29c674b02` (drained s2314), was never added to that list, and the runner swept it into **`f86d3412c` — 13 rows of the gate runner's own telemetry** (re-verified s2317: that commit's `--stat` shows `logs/guard-stats.jsonl | 13 ++++`). ✅ **CODEX DID NOT VIOLATE THE FIREWALL, AND THAT IS THE POINT.** The implementer's report states *"No commit created"* and its final live proof shows `?? logs/guard-stats.jsonl`, untracked. The commit is the RUNNER's. The master's NO list (*"do NOT `git add` it — tracking it is a separate decision that belongs to the finding, not to you"*) and s2315's standing `🚫 BINDING` both bind the implementer, not the shell script that commits on its behalf — **a firewall success wearing a violation's clothes: the discipline held everywhere a human wrote it and failed in the one place nobody had written it down.** ⚠️ **THE INTERACTION IS WHAT EARNS THIS A ROW, AND ITS POLARITY INVERTED UNDER THE VERY CURE IT RODE IN WITH.** Before `858baeb81`, tracking this file produced a **dirty tree** — loud, and exactly what F-2315-1 measured. After it, tracking the file **silently disables the feature**: re-read at source s2317, `scripts/run-guards.mjs:309` classifies the path with `git ls-files --error-unmatch`, and on a tracked verdict `:317` prints `guard-stats: skipped … because it is tracked; a gate must not dirty its own tree` and **appends nothing**, leaving rc untouched. The stats file would freeze at whatever rows it was committed with, **forever, while every gate keeps reporting success.** That is strictly harder to notice than a dirty tree, and it is the same permissive polarity this streak keeps finding: a corpus that stops being written, wearing the shape of a healthy run. ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: the sweep is LIVE — it happened, in this slice, today — but NOTHING REACHED MAIN.** s2316's exclusion held, and `logs/guard-stats.jsonl` is **UNTRACKED on main**, re-verified s2317 by `git ls-files --error-unmatch logs/guard-stats.jsonl` → *"pathspec … did not match any file(s) known to git"*. So no gate has yet gone quiet and every guard-stats green read so far is TRUE. **What earns the corrective is the CLASS, not this instance: any new untracked `logs/*` file the factory invents is swept BY DEFAULT, because the list enumerates by hand what git already knows how to answer** — a hand-maintained list of what git already knows is a defect awaiting the next filename. 🛠️ **RECOMMENDED CURE (not taken by s2316 — runner surface, outside that slice's firewall): ask the question STRUCTURALLY rather than by list — exclude `logs/` wholesale at the lane-commit site, or drive the excludes from `.gitignore`** — so a new factory log cannot arm this simply by being born. ⏳ **NOT FIRE-TAKEN AT s2317 EITHER, FOR A MEASURED REASON RATHER THAN A SHRUG: `scripts/lane-runner-v3.sh` was EXECUTING throughout this fire** (`lantern-show-agent-honesty` dispatched into lane-d at 21:40:52 by an attended session, codex live). **bash reads a script incrementally from disk, so editing a running one can shift the offsets of code it has not yet read; the fix is one line and must land while the runner is IDLE, and the fire that takes it should re-verify with `ps` first.** Its natural owner is a fire that finds an idle board, or an attended session that can restart the runner with `bash scripts/start-lane-runner.sh` in the same breath. ⓘ **GATE: the cure must keep `logs/factory-usage.json` and `logs/usage-history.jsonl` excluded (a wholesale `logs/` exclusion already subsumes both), and must NOT exclude anything outside `logs/` — the runner's evidence commits legitimately carry `artifacts/**` and `reviews/shots-*`.** ⛔ **THAT RECOMMENDED CURE IS MEASURED WRONG — DO NOT APPLY IT. See F-2319-1:** a wholesale `logs/` exclusion also drops `logs/session-scratch/**`, which 14 of the 701 `runner(` commits use to carry **136 files of lane EVIDENCE** (probe specs, raw run JSON, tsc/build output) — a RETENTION LAW hole traded for a hygiene one. The GATE above guarded the wrong boundary: it asked whether the cure reached OUTSIDE `logs/` and never whether `logs/` itself carries lane output. It does. The landed cure is a depth test on the DELTA (`logs/*/*` keeps, `logs/*` withholds), because **no pathspec form can express the distinction** — `:(exclude)logs/`, `:(exclude)logs/*` and `:(exclude,glob)logs/*` all prune the subtree, proven on a scratch repo. ⓘ **Its cited coordinate `:488` is also the ART path, not the lane path** — ordinary lanes commit via `commit_lane_delta`/`lane_dirty_status`, so curing `:488` alone would have left the live path defective.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1004:🔎 **F-2145-1 (s2145 2026-08-21, fire-side, NON-BLOCKING — AN ANSWER, NOT A DEBT): THE WAVE-8 TERMINAL THE CANYON THREAD HAS CALLED `NOT ESTABLISHED` FOR FOUR ATTEMPTS IS ESTABLISHED — `terminalCause: rider-down (dead)`, TERMINAL `hp: 0`.** 🎯 **AND THE INSTRUMENT `f2144-1`'s REPORT ASKED FOR ALREADY EXISTED — I BUILT NOTHING.** That report names the cure as *"a trace or sanctioned harness artifact that emits the terminal `run_ended` event and its `reason` before Gate B throws"*, which reads as a harness change nobody had made; but `scripts/f2142-canyon-terminal-probe.mjs`, written during the s2142 investigation and sitting in `scripts/` ever since, **re-runs the same leg through the same `HeadlessContractSim` loop and reads the terminal state Gate B discards** — read-only, `/tmp` output, no src/player/contract/seed/harness touched. Evidence banked at `artifacts/f2135-canyon-census/terminal-cause-s2145.json` (0.72 MB) with the note `artifacts/f2135-canyon-census/TERMINAL-CAUSE.md`. 📊 **THE TERMINAL, IN FULL:** `{secured:false, waves:8, timeMs:259000, gold:95, kills:126, calls:540, defaultedPicks:6, defaultedSecure:0}`; **59 enemies alive of 185 spawned, 33 of them wreckers**; works **5 `sentry_beacon` + 2 `lantern_post` standing, 2 wrecked**; hero hp first ≤20 at turn 341 (wave 7), 0 during wave 8. `terminal === this.dead || this.secureChoice === 'bank'` (`HeadlessContractSim.ts:1308`), and with `defaultedSecure: 0` and `secured:false` **only `dead` remains** — the run ends because the Prospector goes down, not on any contract condition. ⭐ **THREE CONTROLS BEFORE THE VERDICT WAS BELIEVED, BECAUSE THIS THREAD HAS LOST THREE ATTEMPTS TO CONFIDENT READINGS OF UNDER-DETERMINED EVIDENCE:** (1) the probe was booted at `?debug&contract=e3-canyon-works`, **byte-identical** to the URL the cured harness builds at `gr-sim-campaign.mjs:17`, and its **540 trace rows agree with the census's 540 rows on `wave`/`powered`/`failed` at EVERY turn — 0 mismatches**, so it is provably the same run; (2) `Terrain.CLAIM_WIDTH/HEIGHT` read **96 × 112**, the canyon's authored claim, not the 64 × 64 fallback that WAS the whole of the cured `f2142-1` defect; (3) **all six authored beacon sites are `centreBuildable` AND `centreWalkable`** (four with a fully buildable 2.5 wu disc, 317/317; the two rim sites 245/317) — the ground is not the obstacle. ⚠️ **THIS IS THE MECHANISM AND IT IS WHERE THE FINDING STOPS. Five beacons standing of the six both branches require, two wrecked, 95 g in hand — whether that is under-defended play, an unaffordable rebuild loop, or a contract that cannot be held on this seed is a BALANCE question and stays owner-reserved under `F-E2S-4`, untouched.** `failed:true` remains a measurement, not a verdict (F-2143-2). **GATE C unchanged** — same pinned `benchSeeds[id][0]`, so `e3-canyon-works-02` is still unmeasured. 💡 **THE REUSABLE HALF, and it is the reason this is filed rather than just noted: a report that names the instrument it lacks is describing a CAPABILITY, not a missing file — grep `scripts/` for the capability before anyone authors it.** Four attempts wrote `NOT ESTABLISHED` against a probe that had been committed, cited and sitting in the run surface the entire time; the answer cost one read-only command and no new code. *The same file may already solve the class a new mechanism is proposed for.*
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1439:🔎 **F-SEAL-1 (attended 2026-08-11, MEASURED AT THE CROWN-TAPE BACKFILL — NEGATIVE RESULT THAT SETTLES THE REELS LAW'S SCOPE): Season-1 crowns are SEALED HISTORY — they cannot carry replay-true reels, because the Same-Game era genuinely changed the game.** The agent-reels-2 backfill re-ran the three deterministic crown players with `--tape`; each reproduced itself perfectly — under TODAY'S rules: pi's crown player (secured w10/g50 in its era) now DIES AT WAVE 6 g30 (`bench/gauntlet/tapes/pi-the-claim.json`, outcome reason:death), because the ap16-2b draft lifecycle (offer + 20s trail clock) shifts upgrade timing; `tapeMatchesScore` then rightly refuses a death-tape on a secured row — the exact tapeless-run-in-a-valid-reel fraud F-1617-1 named. ⚖️ **RULING IMPLIED BY THE ERA LAW, no owner word needed: reels are SEASON-2-NATIVE.** Old rows stay tapeless and season-labeled (history, not cheats — the Seasons law verbatim); every NEW standing posts WITH its tape (`gr-sim --tape` ships). The board deployed `d28b3c5a` accepts them. 💡 **The juicy half for the Season-1 page: the parity changes have measurable gameplay teeth — the founding era's winning strategy no longer wins.** The three cross-era tapes are kept in `bench/gauntlet/tapes/` as the first controlled before/after measurement of a rules era. GATE: none — SEA-3 cites this; the reels ladder is COMPLETE as merged.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1824:🔺 **F-DOOR-2 (attended 2026-08-08, ENTRANT-FOUND + VERIFIED AT SOURCE — A REFUSED BUILD SAYS ONLY "FAILED": THE DOOR CANNOT NAME THE CAUSE).** The pi circuit entrant, securing e3-moth-season, hit repeated `FAILED: BUILD action was rejected.` on lantern placements with zero diagnostic and had to probe positions one by one. ✓ VERIFIED: `ToolSurface.ts:67` — `reason` is a 4-value enum (`PERMISSION_DENIED|NO_SYSTEM_API|INVALID_ARGS|FAILED`) and every game-logic refusal (funds, collision, terrain, zone, cap) collapses to `'FAILED'` at `:266`; `StandingOrders.ts:254` then templates it verbatim. An agent cannot distinguish "save more gold" from "this spot is illegal" — the two most different possible next moves. Cure authored: `tasks/lane-fdoor2-rejection-reasons.md` (lane-b ladder, after mp-07a/f-door-1) — additive `detail` on refusal receipts, cause vocabulary documented in skill.md. **GATE: CLOSED — CURED, drained attended 2026-08-08 (review reviews/f-door-2-rejection-reasons.md); the test asserts `FAILED (insufficient_gold): ...` and pins never moved.**
