tasks/BACKLOG.md:1897:✅ **SHIPPED s1507 — `f1506-2-e9-roster-bisect` MERGED `39987a4252dad31fb8ba3d267dde1c288dc6dc42` (review `reviews/f1506-2-e9-roster-bisect.md`). CURES THE E9 ROSTER REGRESSION F-1506-2 WAS AUTHORED TO FIND — AND THE MASTER'S TWO PROHIBITIONS BOTH HELD.** The bisect named first-bad **`f3e2d102694d1c6f1c20a3fa3fcdcca1784d3962`** (`runner(lane-c): lane-tape-02-lantern-show.md`, 15 files / +841 / −41). That commit made `Game.activeEpoch` derive from whichever epoch owns `activeContract`; Seed Run is deliberately unavailable (`harvestAnchors: []`), so **every ordinary boot fell back to the E1 Claim contract** while `E9ArsenalSystem` gates on `activeEpoch.order >= 9` — which is exactly the two observed values, terraform cannon `0` and `eraActive: false`. The cure is three lines at `src/game/Game.ts:634`: contract-derived epochs now ride the **`?replay=` Lantern route alone**, ordinary and debug runs return to `selectActiveEpoch()`. `this.contractEpoch` is untouched and still feeds `e6TileConsumers`. 🚫 **BOTH FORBIDDEN CURES REFUSED, verified by FILE LIST rather than by the report's word:** the diff is exactly `docs/bench/e9-roster-regression.md` (+90) and `src/game/Game.ts` (+3/−1) — `e2e/e9-roster.spec.ts` untouched, red inventory untouched. 🧪 **Gated on the MERGED tree in detached `gate-s1507` (§3.0b), all playwright `--workers=1` (§3.1):** tsc clean 4.1 s · build green 15.5 s · **own spec 6 passed**, matching the GOOD endpoint exactly · **the culprit's own `tape-02-lantern-show` 2 passed**, so the feature f3e2d102 shipped still works · `test:node-guards` rc=0, 345 tests, 342 pass, 0 fail. 📋 **THE ADJACENT DENOMINATOR WAS RE-DERIVED, NOT INHERITED** — this cure moves `activeEpoch` for *every* non-replay boot, so `grep -rln 'eraActive|selectActiveEpoch|activeEpoch|epochOrder|era-active' e2e/` gave **25 non-own specs: 162 tests, 146 passed, 15 failed, 1 skipped, 1157.7 s**. 🔍 **ALL 15 REDS ATTRIBUTED INDIVIDUALLY, AND NONE IS THIS MERGE'S.** Six fingerprint-matched **KNOWN-RED** on title *and* error shape (`e9-arsenal` ×2 at 75% blast radius, `e6-arsenal`, `e2-t2-dynamo-ceremony`, `ui-era-dressing`, `wire-era-anchor-emitters`). Two were **CLEAN-IN-INVENTORY and therefore NOT excused** — controlled instead, at pre-merge `a4556dca5` in the same worktree and composition, where they red **identically** (→ F-1507-2). ⚠️ **A lookup-reading trap worth recording: `red-inventory-lookup`'s LINE 1 IS A HEADER and the verdict is line 2** — my first pass read line 1 and every spec came back looking identical. 🎯 **ONE CANDIDATE SURVIVED TO THE END AND DIED ON THE THIRD MEASUREMENT:** `town-dynamo-hall-blender:97` was red merged / green control, a real 3-vs-4 delta. But it is **6/6 green when run ALONE in both arms**, it reds in the **CONTROL** arm under the same composition, and that control pair returned **3 failed then 6 failed on one fixed commit** with the assertion's own bound moving (`10.2 vs <=10.005` → `18.1 vs <=11.155`). **So the composition's failure count is unstable on a fixed commit, which means a single-run cross-arm comparison was never a valid instrument — including the one that produced the delta** (→ F-1507-3). ⚠️ **A VACUOUS VERDICT WAS CAUGHT ON THE WAY, and it is the most reusable part:** my first attribution script printed *"no new reds attributable to the merge"* while its title regex matched **nothing** — it compared two EMPTY lists and would have printed those words whatever the arms did. The second pass parses playwright's end-of-run failure block and **refuses to conclude** when the tallies report failures but no entries parse. Related: [F-1506-2], [F-1503-3], [F-1507-2], [F-1507-3], [F-1507-1].
tasks/BACKLOG.md:1924:✅ **SUPERSEDED s1506 — SHIPPED as `efb5465dca18c964a69aba8a0d69ead8cf4cf223`, see the row at the top of this file. Original authoring row follows.** ✍️ **F-1501-4 AUTHORED s1505 (FIRE-AUTHORED — attended review welcome) — `tasks/lane-f1501-4-manifest-plural.md` → lane-c, goal leaf `f1501-4-manifest-plural`. THE CLASS-FIX WARNING WAS RIGHT ABOUT THE DENOMINATOR AND WRONG ABOUT THE WORK: 42 CONSUMERS, EXACTLY ONE DEFECTIVE OUTPUT.** F-1501-4 warned that *"a fix is a class fix with 42 consumers"*, which is true — so s1505 **swept all 42 before writing scope** rather than authoring against the warning. The pluraliser (`src/agent/MechanicsManifest.ts:420`, `${humanize(id)}${count === 1 ? '' : 's'}`) emits **five** terms board-wide and **exactly one is wrong**: `straw_man` ×3 → **"straw mans"** (`e1-drill-yard`, via `practice.targets`). Correct and must stay byte-identical: `lantern posts` (×7 `e1-night-shift`, ×2 `e3-blackout-ridge`/`e3-canyon-works`), `rolling logs` (×2 `e1-drill-yard`), `sentry beacons` (×3 `e3-blackout-ridge`), `turrets` (×2 `e3-canyon-works`). `count === 1` appends nothing, so every singular term is **out of scope by construction**. ⇒ the irregular map needs **one entry**, and the master forbids a general English pluraliser as the vocabulary stretch it would be (Mistake #14). ⚠️ **A MEASURING TRAP THAT CAUGHT THE AUTHOR FIRST, WRITTEN INTO THE MASTER SO IT CANNOT CATCH THE RUNNER:** interactable ids reach the pluraliser from **three** sources (`:427-470`) and are **not normalised alike** — `tileParams.prePlacedBuildables` and `practice.stations` use the id **raw**, while `practice.targets` passes `kind` through `toSnakeCase`, which unlike `humanize` **also maps `-` → `_`** (`:486-488`). The Drill Yard authors its targets as `straw-man`/`rolling-log` **with hyphens**, so a sweep that forgets `toSnakeCase` reports `"straw-mans"`/`"rolling-logs"` and sends the runner hunting a hyphen de-slug bug **that does not exist**. The first pass of this very sweep did exactly that; the second mirrored `:482-488` byte-for-byte. ✅ **FIXTURE SAFETY VERIFIED, NOT ASSUMED — and it is what keeps an open owner fork closed:** `e2e/fixtures/e1-mechanics-manifests.json` holds raw ids (`straw_man` **present**) and **never** the rendered sentence (`This claim speaks` **absent from all 7,459 bytes**), so a render-time cure provably cannot move the byte-stable fixture that `f1328-1` is still on the desk about. 🎯 **THE CRUX OF THE MASTER IS THAT THE EXISTING TEST CANNOT SEE THIS BUG.** `e2e/agent-view.spec.ts:348-352` (in **"the derived manifest rides THE VIEW and every E1 briefing speaks it"**, `:297`) asserts the DOM against `mechanicsManifestLine(deriveMechanicsManifest(id))` **computed inside the test** — the renderer against itself. It passed while the card said "straw mans" and would pass again on "straw manss". So scope 2 requires an assertion pinning the **literal** words, and scope 3 requires `rolling logs` as the **sharp control** — the other `practice.targets` entry on the *same card*, currently correct, which goes red if the cure is bought by mangling the general path. Scope 4 orders the defect **manufactured** (revert, prove red, restore) per the s1299/s1301 standard. 📮 Dispatch will run the full F-1424-3 order; the currency key `export function mechanicsManifestLine(manifest: MechanicsManifest): string {` was measured **1 on main** before being written down (F-1425-2), is single-line and apostrophe-free, and is grepped against the SOURCE file rather than the master, so 1 is the honest expectation (F-1502-1). **GATE: closes when the lane-c run drains, the Drill Yard line reads "straw men" in both viewport screenshots, and the other four rendered plurals are proved unmoved.** Related: [F-1501-4], [F-1501-1], [F-1432-4], [f1328-1].
