ntical. ⓘ **The s1428 UNVERIFIED item is now ANSWERED**: the fixtures are **not** `MeshBasicMaterial` by day but **are** at dusk, which is exactly why a single-type check could never work. 🟢 **F-1429-1 (new, non-blocking, laddered) — THE ORDERED CURE IS LOUD IN THE ONE PLACE WHERE LOUDNESS REACHES A PLAYER, AND I MEASURED THE BLAST RADIUS RATHER THAN REASONING ABOUT IT.** The master rightly forbade a silent `return false` and ordered that a guard which cannot see its subject must say so; the runner obeyed literally with a `throw`. **But `townLightDiagnostics()` is not test-only** — it is reached from `publishDiagnostics()` (`src/town/TownScene.ts:2472`), which has **no debug gate** and is called from ~20 sites including the town boot path (`:554`, right after `dressScene()`/`createUi()`), so the throw executes in every normal player session. Today it cannot fire (both fixtures carry `.color`); the hazard is **latent** — a future material swap to a colourless type (`ShaderMaterial`, `MeshDepthMaterial`) turns a *diagnostics* concern into **player-facing town breakage**. I forced the throw and booted the town: `[Unhandled rejection] Error: PROBE-s1429 uninspectable fixture TownPropLanternGlow`, then `Test timeout of 90000ms exceeded` on `page.waitForFunction` — the town **never finishes mounting**, a hung boot rather than a graceful red. Probe reverted. **This is not runner disobedience** — it is the ordered cure meeting a call graph the master did not account for, because the master reasoned about the guard as a test instrument and it is also on the player’s path; it is CLAUDE.md Mistake #10 inverted, debug-only code reaching the player. **Cure (laddered):** report a distinct `uninspectableFixtures` count (or a `-1` sentinel) the specs assert on, so the guard still cannot silently report `0` while the town still boots. 🚫 **Do NOT “cure” F-1429-1 by restoring `return false`** — that re-opens F-1428-2 exactly.
