tasks/BACKLOG.md:2537:✅ **F-1319-4 CLOSED — ap-07-night-shift-fixtures SHIPPED s1319 at `07854e6b`**, review `reviews/ap-07-night-shift-fixtures.md`, authored AND drained the same fire (stated as the conflict of interest it is; every certifying measurement was reproduced independently rather than read). `e1-night-shift` is admitted to GR-SIM **and its seven wrecked `lantern_post` fixtures are placed first**, by a generic `prePlacedBuildables ?? []` loop with **no contract branch** — so the agent is no longer briefed and manifested about seven objects absent from its world. ✓ **Every pre-declared REJECT condition survived MY OWN reproduction, not the runner’s report:** the assertion derives the count from `contract.tileParams.prePlacedBuildables.length` (no hand-typed `7`); I neutered the loop myself and got **`undefined !== 7`, 2 pass / 1 fail**, and the byte-exact restore returned sha256 `9f7fb225…f5cf` — **the same hash the runner reported**. `docs/bench/agent-playability-census.md`’s undifferentiated *"objective drivers for night-shift, twin-banks, and baron"* sentence is corrected (**AGENT-READY 2 of 41 → 3 of 41**); night-shift needed no driver, only fixtures. Gates: tsc clean · build green · `gr-sim` + `bench-seeds` **5/5** · node-guards **204 → 205**, delta explicable. Original row, retained for history: ~~🔨 **QUEUED (s1319, FIRE-AUTHORED — attended review welcome) → lane-b: `tasks/lane-b-ap07-night-shift-fixtures.md`. AP-07: ADMIT `e1-night-shift` TO GR-SIM — BUT PLACE ITS SEVEN LANTERNS FIRST, BECAUSE THE PIN IS NOT THE ONLY THING IN THE WAY.** ✓ **VERIFIED AT SOURCE s1319, every number re-derived this fire.** The gate is clear: `specs/agent-play/README.md` rehearsal-gates **AP-03/04/05 only** and says verbatim *"GR-SIM itself is engine work, buildable now"* — AP-07 sits outside it. `src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` admits two contracts and scores **both** by one generic rule (reach `twist.secureWave` alive) with **no contract branch anywhere in the file**. **`e1-night-shift` is the only remaining E1 contract that shares that property**, measured across all five: `briefing.goals[0]` = *"Survive to DAWN at wave 25."* against `twist.secureWave` **25**, and **zero `stakeMarkers`** — so the F-1314-1 inert-`lossCondition` blocker that genuinely gates `e1-twin-banks` (2 markers) **does not apply**. `e1-baron` stays out: *"Break his Rocket Cart"* is not survival, and a literal lift would reproduce the twin-banks scoring lie. ⚠️ **THE REAL FINDING, AND THE REASON THIS IS NOT A ONE-LINE PIN-LIFT: night-shift is the ONLY E1 contract with `tileParams.prePlacedBuildables` — seven wrecked `lantern_post`, `relightCost: 8` — and `grep -c prePlacedBuildables src/sim/HeadlessContractSim.ts` is `0`.** Meanwhile `src/agent/MechanicsManifest.ts` publishes those same seven fixtures to the agent as `relight` interactables and the contract’s own `briefing.rules` says *"Relight cold lanterns or build new posts to see threats."* ➡️ **A bare pin-lift would brief and manifest seven objects into a world containing none — the F-1314-1 defect one layer up.** Unlike twin-banks it needs no invented mechanic: `Game.ts::placeContractFixtures()` is a five-line reference implementation, and the transplant must stay contract-branch-free (`?? []` leaves the other contracts untouched). ⚖️ **Scope 1 is observe-first and can CANCEL** — night-shift has **never** been probed headless (s1314/s1315 covered `the-claim` and `e1-twin-banks` only), so a crash or malformed outcome is a live engine defect and a bigger finding than the one the task was sent for. **Scope 4’s acceptance condition is a manufactured RED**, because the new fixture assertion is green the moment the transplant lands *including if it is written wrong* (the f1297-2 shape); **a hand-typed `7` instead of `tileParams.prePlacedBuildables.length` is a pre-declared REJECT** (F-1318-1’s lesson: certify the producer’s contract, not today’s value). ⛔ `eval_dataset.jsonl` rows and the `num_examples` order