tasks/BACKLOG.md:2539:🟡 **F-1319-3 (s1319, MEASURED BY ME ON BOTH ARMS — PLACING SEVEN FIXTURES COSTS 8.6× THE ENTIRE HEADLESS RUN, AND THAT TAX LANDS ON THE ONE PROPERTY AP-07 EXISTS FOR).** Same machine, same seed `e1-night-shift-01`, only the fixture loop differing: **fixtures neutered 2,306 ms → fixtures placed 19,900 ms = 8.63×.** The runner independently measured 2,610 → 21,429 ms (**8.21×**) — same magnitude on a differently-loaded box. ✓ **Both arms’ `eventLogHash` values reproduced the runner’s EXACTLY** (`fnv1a32:84c22e10` without, `fnv1a32:c086ef19` with), so the before/after table is fully independently confirmed and `secured`/`waves`/`timeMs`/`gold`/`kills`/`calls` are unchanged between arms — **the lanterns are truth-bearing but not load-bearing under the idle policy.** ⚠️ **Why this is not cosmetic:** `specs/agent-play/README.md` states AP-07’s premise verbatim — *"Browser-free = fast parallel rollouts (RL-scale)"*. An ~8.6× per-episode cost is a direct tax on the only property that makes the headless runner worth building, and night-shift is the contract an RL loop would most want (25 waves, the longest E1 episode). ⚠️ **And it is already near a hard limit:** the new `scripts/gr-sim.test.mjs` night-shift case sets `timeout: 30_000` against a **19.9 s** run — ~10 s of headroom on an *idle* box. Under any concurrent load this becomes a plausible flake **that fails as a timeout**, i.e. it will read like an engine hang rather than a budget overrun, and will be triaged accordingly. ⓘ **Cause NOT localised, and I am saying so rather than guessing.** Two candidates: `placeFree`’s per-fixture cost in a headless `BuildSystem` (one-off, at construction) versus seven extra `wrecked` structures widening every targeting/combat scan across **3,785 ticks** (per-tick, and therefore *scaling with episode length* — which would make it worst for exactly the longest contracts). **These predict different fixes and the measurement that separates them is cheap.** ➡️ **FIRE-AUTHORABLE AS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A CURE, and not owner-gated:** profile one night-shift run, attribute the delta between construction-time and per-tick cost, and only then choose. Raising the test timeout without doing this would hide the finding rather than fix it. 💡 *The reusable shape: **a correctness fix can bill its cost to a different budget than the one it was reviewed against.** This slice fixed a real lie — an agent briefed about objects that did not exist — and paid for it in the throughput property its own spec names as its reason to exist. Neither the master nor the bar asked about wall time; the runner volunteered it, and it is the most consequential number in the run.* GATE: none. No goal leaf yet. ✅ **ANSWERED s1320 — and BOTH of the two candidate causes named above are REFUTED by measurement. The real cause is `terrainSeed()` re-parsing the URL on every noise hash; see the F-1320-1 row directly below, which supersedes this row's diagnosis (but not its numbers, which reproduced exactly).** ✅ **CURED AND SHIPPED s1321 at `992f40661abb437faba6fc2a7ddb8c5f6706f7db`** (review `reviews/f1319-3-terrain-seed-per-sample-url-parse.md`) — the search-keyed cache, i.e. the SAFE of the two cures F-1320-1 measured. Gated `--workers=1`: tsc clean, build 1.90s, new guard green desktop 4.1s + mobile 4.2s zero console errors, **node-guards 205/205 fail 0 including `gr-sim` byte-for-byte replay so determinism is preserved**, Night Shift fixtures **6,635 ms vs ~19.9 s**, terrain3d-default + never-trap 5/5. ⭐ **The guard has TEETH, proven by MUTATION not argument:** reverting `terrainSeed()` to its pre-cure form reds the new spec **Expected 1 / Received 5600** — 28 `URLSearchParams` constructions per `sampleHeight`, independently corroborating the ~36-per-sample attribution — and the tree was restored byte-exact (sha256 `4ec3c755e2c59feb` both sides). It asserts a MECHANISM (derivation count), not wall time, so it cannot be defused by raising a timeout.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:2541:🟡 **F-1320-1 — struck s1344, history only (cured by `992f4066`, 2026-08-01T08:49).** ✓ RE-VERIFIED AT SOURCE, not inherited: `terrainSeed()` (`src/world/Terrain.ts:1619-1624`) now memoises through `terrainSeedCache`, keyed on `window.location.search`, and re-parses **only when that string changes** — the per-call `new URLSearchParams` the finding describes is GONE. Cure commit's own message: *"cache the terrain seed per URL search string — 28 URLSearchParams constructions per sampleHeight become 1"*. ⚠️ **F-1319-3 (line 60) is DELIBERATELY LEFT OPEN: its claim is a measured 8.6× fixture-cost RATIO, and I did not re-run that measurement.** The root cause is cured; the ratio is unverified, and striking a parent finding on a child's evidence is exactly how a real red gets closed by inference. ⓘ **This row is the specimen for F-1344-2** (an open 🟡 whose defect was cured in CODE with no closure row anywhere — `findings-state-guard` compares ledger to ledger and is structurally blind to it; double-state was 0 the whole time). ORIGINAL FINDING, retained verbatim: 🟡 **F-1320-1 (s1320, ROOT CAUSE OF F-1319-3 — THE TERRAIN SEED IS RE-PARSED FROM THE URL ON EVERY NOISE HASH, AND IT IS NOT A HEADLESS PROBLEM).** `terrainSeed()` (`src/world/Terrain.ts:1619-1622`) derives the run seed by constructing **a new `URLSearchParams` from `window.location.search` and re-running `normalizeSeed`** — *on every call*. `terrainHash()` (`:1636`) calls it once per hash, `valueNoise()` (`:1624`) calls `terrainHash` **four times**, and `sample()`/`terrainFeatures()` call `valueNoise` ~9 times: **one terrain sample costs roughly 36 URL parses.** 🔬 **A `--cpu-prof` of one `e1-night-shift` episode (19.85 s, 2,618 samples) attributes ~67% of the run to URL parsing:** `parseParams` **41.4% / 8,218 ms**, `normalizeSeed` 14.1% / 2,790 ms, `URLSearchParams` ctor 9.0% / 1,782 ms, `get search` 2.6% / 516 ms — with `terrainHash` (7.1%) and `terrainSeed` (4.2%) as the callers. ⚠️ **Both of F-1319-3's hypotheses are refuted, and I measured rather than argued.** Construction/`placeFree` cost: `nonTickMs` is **indistinguishable between arms** (801–949 ms with zero fixtures, 482–1,178 ms with seven) — refuted. Structure count: seven *working* lanterns cost **+970 ms**, but flipping **those same seven** to `wrecked` costs a further **+16,730 ms** — so the count is ~6% of the delta and `wrecked` is ~94%. Wrecked fixtures were never the disease; they are the symptom that made it *measurable*, because wrecked instances alone fall through `updateRepairs`' cheap `continue` (`BuildSystem.ts:2117`) into `terrainMaxForFootprint` **every tick**. ⚡ **THE CONSEQUENTIAL HALF: this is not headless-only.** `terrainSeed()` early-outs only on `typeof window === 'undefined'`; **in a browser `window` is always defined**, so the shipped game pays the same ~36-parses-per-sample on every terrain sample — including `Terrain.sample`, which the hero ground-height lookup calls **every frame**. The headless runner did not create this cost, it merely has no frame budget to hide it in. 📐 **Cure measured BOTH ways on the merged tree, both bit-for-bit determinism-preserving (`eventLogHash` stayed `fnv1a32:c086ef19`, `timeMs` `126167`, identical tick count 3,785):** search-keyed cache **19,048 → 3,704 ms (5.1×)**, drop-in and self-invalidating; naive memoise-once **19,048 → 2,174 ms (8.8×)** but requires explicit invalidation at the four `replaceState`/`pushState` seed-rewriting sites (`main.ts:204/219`, `DebugEraSeed.ts:35`, `DeterminismHarness.ts:68`, `TownScene.ts:1143`). **Recommendation: the search-keyed cache** — 5.1× for four lines, and a missed invalidation site in the faster option produces *wrong terrain*, which is far worse than 1.5 s. ⓘ Both s1319 arms' hashes (`84c22e10`, `c086ef19`) reproduced exactly, so its before/after table is independently confirmed; the tree was restored byte-exact after every probe (`git diff -- src/` empty). ➡️ **QUEUED s1320 as `lane-d-f1319-3-terrain-seed-per-sample-url-parse.md`** (goal leaf `f1319-3-terrain-seed-per-sample-url-parse` under `agent-play`, same commit). 💡 *The reusable shape: **the profiler disagreed with both hypotheses, and both hypotheses were reasonable.** F-1319-3 named two candidates from reading the diff — per-fixture construction cost vs per-tick scan widening — and the honest answer was a third thing neither the master nor the review had any reason to suspect, sitting four lines deep in a file the slice never touched. **One `--cpu-prof` cost less than the reasoning did.*** GATE: none — fire-authorable, not owner-gated. ✅ **CURED AND SHIPPED s1321 at `992f40661abb437faba6fc2a7ddb8c5f6706f7db`** (review `reviews/f1319-3-terrain-seed-per-sample-url-parse.md`) — the search-keyed cache, i.e. the SAFE of the two cures F-1320-1 measured. Gated `--workers=1`: tsc clean, build 1.90s, new guard green desktop 4.1s + mobile 4.2s zero console errors, **node-guards 205/205 fail 0 including `gr-sim` byte-for-byte replay so determinism is preserved**, Night Shift fixtures **6,635 ms vs ~19.9 s**, terrain3d-default + never-trap 5/5. ⭐ **The guard has TEETH, proven by MUTATION not argument:** reverting `terrainSeed()` to its pre-cure form reds the new spec **Expected 1 / Received 5600** — 28 `URLSearchParams` constructions per `sampleHeight`, independently corroborating the ~36-per-sample attribution — and the tree was restored byte-exact (sha256 `4ec3c755e2c59feb` both sides). It asserts a MECHANISM (derivation count), not wall time, so it cannot be defused by raising a timeout.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:2603:🟠 **F-1313-2 (s1313, RE-DERIVED AT SOURCE — THE BT-04 CLAIM IS FALSE AS WORDED, AND THE TRUE VERSION MOVES IT FROM FIRE-AUTHORABLE TO OWNER-GATED).** s1312 handed forward: *BT-04’s endless mode — its policy switches shipped via M4-07; the consumer never did.* ✗ **FALSIFIED.** The five consent abilities shipped, and **three of them have live plain-boot consumers**: `auto_collect` gates the autonomous gold and XP sweeps, `auto_repair` gates the repair sweep, `light_duty` gates the lantern. **Exactly one is dead — `auto_pan`** — and it is dead structurally, not accidentally: the gate helper’s own parameter type in `Game.ts` lists only the other three, so no game-loop caller can even ask about it, and **there is no autonomous pan loop to gate in the first place.** ✗ **AND THE ENDLESS HALF SHIPPED UNDER ANOTHER NAME:** the word *endless* appears **zero times in `src/` and `e2e/`**; the flow exists as `RunManager.stayForRush()`, wired to a button and capturing a suspend write — delivered by M3-02. **So “the consumer never did [ship]” collapses two unlike facts into one wrong sentence.** ⚠️ **What a player sees today:** at permission rung 2+, the checkbox *Let the Prospector work claim pans* renders and **unchecking it changes nothing**, because nothing auto-pans. ⛔ **NOT FIRE-AUTHORABLE — four design forks, none answered by the spec:** (1) what X is in *auto-repair under X%* (the loop today repairs at any damage, and the panel has only checkboxes, so a numeric policy is new UI); (2) what *idle* means for auto-pan, and where the Prospector pans; (3) **the spec’s own Law 4 — *production ramp must never make endless trivially safe* — makes an autonomous gold engine a BALANCE ruling, not a wiring task**, the same design-adjacency that firewalled steal-pressure out of BT-02b; (4) whether consent should gate direct tool calls at all. ⓘ **Also measured: BT-04 has no goal leaf and no review file** — it is neither shipped nor blocked, merely unregistered, so no sweep would ever have surfaced it. ✅ **LEAF REGISTERED s1354** as `bt-04-homestead-automation` under `e1-frontier` (following `bt-02b-stockpile-tiers`, whose own note flags that home as PROVISIONAL), `status: blocked`, all four forks quoted into its `blockedReason` together with the *not-simply-unshipped* correction, so the next fire re-derives none of it. ⚠️ **MEASURED LIMIT: it carries no `taskFile` — because no BT-04 master exists — and `goal-closure-reason.test.mjs` defines a leaf as *any node carrying `taskFile`*, so it is DOCUMENTATION, NOT ENFORCEMENT: `drain-block-check --all` reports 280 scanned / 5 BLOCKED both before and after (564 id-bearing nodes, 280 with `taskFile`). It stops nothing, which costs nothing while there is no master to stop.** The review file is still absent and that is correct — nothing shipped. ⓘ The fork-free residue is one type-union widening that **compiles and changes nothing**, because it has no caller. 💡 *Reusable shape: **“the consumer never shipped” is a claim with a denominator.** Counted per-switch it was 1 of 5, and the one turned out to need an owner ruling rather than a wire.* ⏱️ **RE-MEASURED s1336 — CORE STILL TRUE, ONE CLAUSE NARROWLY FALSE (F-1336-4).** `prospectorCan` (`Game.ts:5874`) still types only `auto_collect | auto_repair | light_duty`, so `auto_pan` stays structurally unaskable on the game loop. ✗ But *"unchecking it changes nothing"* is false on the orders path: `StandingOrders.ts:419` maps HARVEST → `auto_pan` and denies it. True only in a plain boot — the frame it was measured in. Fork **(4)** is F-1313-3's question restated.
