s her the news desk, but `tf-mei` is the F-1120-1 outlier at ~104 vs the 130–145 band — aging it forward either propagates the drift or silently repaints a shipped face: a decision, not a chore). ❌ **CORRECTED IN THE SAME BREATH IT WAS WRITTEN — s1160 attempt 1 claimed this master "discharges F-1154-2". IT DOES NOT: F-1154-2 was already CLOSED at s1155**, and the master copied F-1154-2's *proposed* band (130–145) which s1155 had measured and **rejected**. `assets/LEDGER.md` row 60 verbatim: *"F-1154-2 recommended 'TL+TR, band 130–145' and **that band is WRONG** — it retroactively fails two accepted portraits, `tf-preacher` (124.5, from the very batch that defined the convention) and `tf-appliance-wrangler` (124.6)"*; the pinned rule is **statistic = mean R−B over TL+TR 60×60, GATE = flag below 120**, accepted range 124–145. ✅ **The master's OWN mandatory instrument-control caught this at pre-flight (`49d49007`) before a single `image_gen` call** — the runner measured `tf-preacher` at 124.5, refused to proceed, generated nothing and modified nothing (`tasks/runs/20260728-095121-art-e7-town-icons-preflight.md`; a model stop). **RE-AUTHORED s1160 as attempt 2 with a changed premise:** the gate is now the 120 floor, and the control's expected table is the six *measured* E1 values (137.8 / 134.0 / 105.3 / 124.5 / 140.4 / 143.9) with **exactly one** flag (`tf-mei`), re-verified against row 60 rather than taken from the runner's word. F-1154-3 honoured too: the sheet's order must be **proven by a 5×5 pairing matrix with the 20 wrong pairings as positive control**, never asserted. Reference-tier: extraction WITHHELD (no consumer) → no gazette, no deploy. ✅ **DRAINED s1161 — `art-e7-town-icons` SHIPPED at `7873eaee17e1f4f9e9fcf4575e7aec3e33910f83`** (review `reviews/art-e7-town-icons.md`, goal leaf `e7-art-town-icons` → shipped in the drain commit; **guards 8/8**). ⚠️ **The ART slot commits straight to MAIN's own tree, so this was a GATE-AND-BLESS, not a merge** — there is no lane branch, and the content was already on main when the drain began; the drain's job was to decide whether it earns its place, not to graft it. **The binding gate ran FIRST and passed** (s1160 item 3): the instrument reproduced all six pinned E1 warmth values to **≤0.05 drift** and flagged **exactly** `tf-mei` at **105.3** — so the E7 numbers are admissible. All five portraits **127.5–144.4**, above the 120 floor and inside the accepted 124–145; all six deliverables 1254×1254 RGB, **0 alpha / 0 transparent / 0 exact-magenta / 0 near-magenta**; the runner's own five warmth figures reproduce to **≤0.04**, i.e. it measured honestly. 🔑 **Sheet order re-proven with a DIFFERENT instrument than the runner's:** the run reported true-pairing MAE **0.00**, which is near-tautological because the sheet is a programmatic composite of the same resized raws — re-slicing with the same resampler must return the same bytes. Re-run under a **`nearest` kernel** it is **5/5 bijective**, true pairings **12.25–15.87** vs the twenty wrong-pairing positive controls **32.28–39.61** (×2.1–3.2, no overlap). Firewall PASS: every art blob is **NEW**, **no existing `tf-*` modified** (so the byte-identical E1/E6 source claim is verified structurally, not merely quoted), zero `src/`/`e2e/`/`assets/processed/`, no `icons-e7`, **no CHALK** (correctly withheld per F-1160-1). Canon §9/ADR-001 clean at full size: the canon-risk atom **the keeper's drone is a rounded brass dovecote-BIRD with teal glass lens eyes — no barrel, muzzle, bore, mount, blade or aimed form**; the tape courier is a warm, safe, fully-clothed child; no letters/numerals/logos anywhere. The defector era-EDIT holds identity superbly (same face, hair wave/part, three-quarter angle, half-smile, mint suit; catalog removed, **exactly one** new element = an aged-brass collar jack). tsc clean · build 1.72s. **Playwright deliberately NOT run, and the reason is on the record:** this slice has **no consumer** (`grep -rn 'tf-' src/` still returns only `utf-8` in `CharterShare.ts:43`), so there is no runtime surface to exercise, and lane-d was concurrently running the 2396-test `suite-red-inventory` whose entire value is an accurate red list (Mistake #12). Reference tier ⇒ extraction WITHHELD, **no gazette item** (filter law working), **no deploy**. 🆕 **F-1161-1 (non-blocking):** the era read in this series **lives in the PROPS, not the face** — the defector's eight-year jump is carried by the catalog→collar-jack swap; the greying and brow lines are invisible at the 120px the convention is specified for. Any future transform that changes no prop will read as no transform at all. 🆕 **F-1161-2 (non-blocking, instrument note):** `tf-drone-keeper-e7` has the batch's widest TL/TR spread — **132.5 / 122.5, 10.0 points** — with TR alone under the 124 accepted floor while the pinned mean (127.5) passes comfortably. This is exactly the volatility that made s1155 pin the *mean of both* corners, so the guard behaved as designed; recorded because it is the second batch to show it, and a third would argue for bounding the spread as well as the mean. ➡️ **LADDER ADVANCE (s1161): `art-e8-town-icons` AUTHORED + QUEUED (`tasks/art-e8-town-icons.md`, goal leaf `e8-art-town-icons` in the same commit) — the THIRD rung of the class the owner unblocked on 2026-07-27.** The *"E8 town-icons still owner-blocked on the portrait convention"* text above is the F-1044-4 unshipped-proof and is **now retired**; ✓ file-probe s1161 confirms `git ls-files` returns **zero** `tf-*-e8.png` and zero `icons-e8.png`. ✓ The unblock ruling's line number was **re-verified by grep this fire (`:979`), not inherited** — the E7 master cited a pre-edit `:977`. 🔑 **AND THIS RUNG CARRIES ITS OWN SECOND BLOCKER TOO — s1160's lesson held a third time, so the batch is 4 portraits, not 5.** `specs/epoch-saga/e8-orbital-bundle.md:11` names five townsfolk, but one of them — *"the He-3 assayer **(assay lineage)**"* — sits on an unresolved canon fork → **OWNE