tasks/BACKLOG.md:4904:  ✅ **DRAINED s1428.** Review `reviews/era-true-lights.md`. `townEraAccents` (`src/town/TownScene.ts:3383`) keys the grammar by era order — E1/E2 **flame** (unlit brown `#b97a3d` by day, `#ffb45c` after dusk, gentle 0.055 flicker), E3+ the steady **arc** read (`#bfe8ff`/`#d5efff`, `flickerDepth: 0`) earned from authored Voltage hardware; fixtures, string beads, window/door panes and the six capped PointLights all draw from the table instead of hardcoded cream/white literals. Gates (detached worktree `gate-s1428`, §3.0b, `--workers=1` per §3.1): tsc 0 · build green · **beauty-town 6/6** both projects · **town-era-switch 14/14** both projects · console/page errors asserted `[]` in-spec · contact sheets in `artifacts/era-lights/`. Both code paths **LANE-TOUCHED only** (main moved neither since base `827c2fd1`). ⭐ **NON-VACUITY PROVED BY MANUFACTURED RED, NOT BY THE GREEN (s1299/s1300):** I gave E1 an electric cool-white lantern glass on the merged tree — the exact thing the owner forbids — and the day test went red on `fixtureColor` (`#b97a3d` → `#f2f6ff`) while dusk and Voltage stayed green. Probe reverted, source byte-identical. **The era grammar is genuinely defended.** 🔬 **F-1428-2 (new, non-blocking, laddered) — THE ONE ASSERTION THAT MOST DIRECTLY ENCODES THE OWNER'S WORDS IS VACUOUS, AND THE SAME PROBE IS WHAT EXPOSED IT.** When the fixture went electric, `fixtureColor` reddened but **`coolWhiteEmissiveFixtures` stayed `0`** — the counter carrying *"audit all glow elements / never electric"*. A zero has two very different explanations, so I measured both: reporting `fixtures.length * 1000` returned **2000** (denominator **non-empty** — both `TownPropLanternGlow` and `TownLanternStringBeads` exist by day), while reporting `basicMaterialCount * 1000` returned **0** (**zero of those two are `MeshBasicMaterial` by day**). `TownScene.ts:2548` opens `if (!material.isMeshBasicMaterial) return false;`, so every fixture is filtered out **before its colour is ever examined**: the count is structurally `0` for *any* colour, including an electric one, and it is asserted **only** in the day test. **Cure (laddered):** examine the material the fixtures actually carry rather than early-returning on type, and assert it at **dusk** too, where fixtures are lit — **acceptance must be a manufactured electric fixture that turns the counter non-zero**, or the cure reproduces the same vacuity one layer down. ⚠️ **UNVERIFIED and deliberately not assumed:** whether the fixtures are `MeshBasicMaterial` at *dusk* was not measured; the cure must establish it. 🚫 Do **not** "cure" F-1428-2 by deleting the counter — the owner's clause needs a real guard, not one fewer.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:4947:  - ✅ **lane-e1-perf-pass SHIPPED PARTIAL s1440 — `d60adf88d6683def6bc8aee139dfa477809cf01b` — F-BW-11 answered on the code, its own spec WITHHELD.** Owner, gate walk 2026-08-03, verbatim: *"the light effects are hard on the machine. But we can do some optimization of the threejs of the maps in E1 maybe? I hear there are instanced meshes that should make things faster? We did not really optimize yet but the night map is rough."* The runner **profiled first and optimized second, in cost order, and reported its negative result honestly**: enemy sprite instancing removed ~60 draw calls from the Night pressure scene but changed transparent overlap ordering and **failed pixel equivalence, so it was fully reverted**. What landed is render-path allocation hygiene: `Game.ts` keeps a **rolling frame-window total and reuses a p95 sort buffer** instead of allocating a copy and rescanning every rendered frame; `pools.ts` computes each enemy's **physical light ONCE per render sync** and shares it with watch paint and fever presentation instead of recomputing it three times, and reuses its light-dimming source records; `LightField`/`LightRig`/`Terrain3dClaimPilot` reuse owned arrays and the 32-source candidate buffer instead of `filter`+`sort`+`slice` per render. **Sim, Balance, watchdog thresholds and accepted pixels all untouched** — the runner changed no threshold and said why (night pressure p95 is 54%/58% of the 33.4 ms shed line). 🚫 **WITHHELD: `e2e/e1-perf-pass.spec.ts` (F-1440-2) — it does not measure its `before` arm in-run, it READS IT FROM A COMMITTED ARTIFACT (`census-before-<project>.json`, `:239`) and `STAGE` defaults to `after` (`:8`), so every future run on every machine compares its own wall-clock and draw calls against numbers one lane shell recorded on an M4 Max. It is NOT in `claimedByAnotherConfig` and `testDir: './e2e'` sweeps everything, so merging it would add a permanently-red suite to the shared default battery — red-inventory entry