% of the doctrine's whole 100k budget is not a cost dimension.** 🔺 **F-ER02-2 (P0) THERE IS NO NO-OP:** every turn forces `submit_orders` and every submission REPLACES the record set, so the doctrine's own winning shape (*one plan at the gate, then answer HOLD*) is unavailable, and `calls` measures the protocol, not the rider — **20 rider calls vs 34–38 submissions on the card; 3 vs 341 on a probe (113×)**. 🔺 **F-ER02-3 (P0) THE RATIFIED TIER PAIR IS UNREACHABLE FROM THE SHIPPED CLI:** `--preset`/`--difficulty` → `Unknown argument` (`gr-sim.mjs:87`), and `applyStoredDifficultyPreset()` is called from **exactly one place in the repo, `src/main.ts:130`**. The vein-hunter arm therefore ran in-process through the game's OWN read+apply path (precedent `e2e/mp-balance-harness.spec.ts:41-49` ("seeded rider simulations are deterministic and obey balance invariants")), **licensed by a control proving the in-process transport equals the CLI byte-for-byte — same `eventLogHash` `fnv1a32:9cc451af` and `c80f182d`.** CURE = 3 lines. 🔺 **F-ER02-4 (P1) AND 2 OF VEIN-HUNTER'S 3 LEVERS ARE INERT IN THAT DOOR ANYWAY:** `xp.perKill` (the headless hero never levels — no `Progression`, no `hero.applyStats`, `progression.stats` an all-ones literal at `HeadlessContractSim.ts:715-724`) and `offers.investBonus` (only consumer `Progression.ts:289-291`, never loaded). **Only `enemy.hp` 25.2→28 bites — outcomes were IDENTICAL at both tiers on both seeds.** 🔺 **F-ER02-5 (P0) THE SECURE CONDITION IS GEOMETRICALLY UNREACHABLE:** the headless hero never moves (`IDLE_INTENTS`, `:425`) and **both maps park it at exactly 12.0 wu from the rail its own wave-12 Railcar rides, against `sparkRig.range` 10** — trestle `(12,-12)` vs x=0, incline `(-24,-18)` vs x=-12. It finished every trestle run at **100/100 HP, never touched**. 🔺 **F-ER02-6 (P0) THE WORKS ARE 0.4-SECOND CONSUMABLES:** a 50-gold / 50-HP turret placed at t=105.7 s was wrecked at **t=106.1 s**; **0 standing at the end of all 8 metered runs**, 